## Finding 2 — No Security-Related HTTP Headers (OWASP A05: Security Misconfiguration)

**Severity: 🟠 Medium**

Express, by default, sends an `X-Powered-By: Express` header, advertising your tech stack to attackers. More critically, no security headers (CSP, HSTS, etc.) are set.

```
# ❌ Response headers from the current app include:
X-Powered-By: Express
# (and no Content-Security-Policy, no X-Frame-Options, etc.)
```

**Recommendation:** Use `helmet`, which sets a suite of protective headers in one line:

```js
const helmet = require('helmet');

// ✅ Add near the top, before any routes
app.use(helmet());
// This automatically sets:
//   X-DNS-Prefetch-Control, X-Frame-Options, X-Content-Type-Options,
//   Strict-Transport-Security, Content-Security-Policy, and more.
//   It also removes X-Powered-By.
```

