## Finding 6 — No CORS Policy (OWASP A01: Broken Access Control)

**Severity: 🟠 Medium**

Without an explicit CORS configuration, browsers will apply the same-origin policy — but this only protects browser clients. Server-to-server calls are unrestricted. When a frontend is added, developers often add `cors()` with `origin: '*'` as a quick fix, which is dangerous.

