### 8. No Centralized Error Handling

**The problem:** Unhandled errors in Express will leak stack traces (file paths, library versions, internal logic) to the client by default.

```js
// ❌ CURRENT — no error handler; Express default dumps stack trace to client
```

**The fix:** Add a global error handler and an async wrapper.

```js
// ✅ RECOMMENDED — centralized error handler (must be last middleware)
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log internally with full detail
  console.error({
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    url: req.url,
    method: req.method,
  });

  // Send sanitized response — never expose stack traces
  const status = err.status || err.statusCode || 500;
  res.status(status).json({
    error: status < 500 ? err.message : 'An internal error occurred',
  });
});

// Catch unhandled async errors in routes
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason) => {
  console.error('Unhandled Rejection:', reason);
});
```

