### 9. No HTTPS Enforcement

**The problem:** The app binds to port 3000 over plain HTTP. Credentials and tokens sent to this server are transmitted in cleartext.

```js
// ✅ RECOMMENDED — enforce HTTPS via redirect (when behind a load balancer/proxy)
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (req.headers['x-forwarded-proto'] !== 'https' && process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production') {
    return res.redirect(301, `https://${req.headers.host}${req.url}`);
  }
  next();
});

// OR use HSTS header (via helmet) so browsers always use HTTPS after first visit:
app.use(helmet.hsts({ maxAge: 31536000, includeSubDomains: true }));
```

